Ticket #4471 is marked **known** as one bug: the shared parser reads dates month first and
our tenants write the day first. Reading the merged reports by tenant — not by the intake
tag, which is only a guess from the reporter's browser — the ticket holds **two causes**.

## What is in #4471

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The ticket's own cause is `parser`: the shared parser reads a date month first, a day-first
tenant's people write the day first, and every date lands flipped. That is most of the
ticket, from every tenant we have on file.

The rest is `hint` and does not belong to this ticket: three day-first tenants run
`booking-v3`, whose date field prints `MM/DD/YYYY`. Their people type what the hint tells
them, month first, and the form reads the date the tenant's way — a different bug, with no
ticket of its own. It is filed here: [parser bug](https://github.com/kamil-zbroniec/md13/issues/1),
[hint bug](https://github.com/kamil-zbroniec/md13/issues/2).

<Callout>
The intake tag is not the cause. It is guessed from the reporter's browser at intake. The
cause depends on the tenant's locale and booking form, so it is decided by tenant, not by tag.
</Callout>

## Counting

The export's pages overlap, so one id can come twice. Numbers on this page count unique
reports: one id, one report.

## Footnote

Five reports the desk read as a one-day move (id list in `desk-notes.json`) are counted
where they were filed, under `parser` by tenant.
